cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Multi-GPU Conjugate Gradient Solver with Stencil-Aware SpMV and Compute-Communication Overlap"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bouhrour"
    given-names: "Stéphane"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sbouhrour/mgpu-cg-stencil-solver"
url: "https://sbouhrour.github.io/mgpu-cg-stencil-solver/"
abstract: >-
  Multi-GPU Conjugate Gradient solver (CUDA and MPI) specialized for
  structured stencil grids: 5-point 2D, 7-point and 27-point 3D. On 8x
  NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB: stencil SpMV 2.08x faster than the cuSPARSE CSR
  of CUDA 12.8; CG 1.41x faster than NVIDIA AmgX on 1 GPU and 1.44x on 8
  GPUs at equal algorithm (both unpreconditioned); 93.5% strong scaling
  efficiency in 2D and 88% in 3D (27-point, compute-communication overlap).
keywords:
  - CUDA
  - MPI
  - multi-GPU
  - conjugate gradient
  - sparse matrix-vector multiplication
  - stencil
  - A100
